1
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:03,100
"Kiss Or Kill"

2
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,000
(Episode 5)

3
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:32,959
Going to the bathroom? I'll join you.

4
00:01:34,599 --> 00:01:36,679
Pack up. It's time to go.

5
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:37,680
So soon?

6
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:40,920
It's almost dawn.

7
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,079
Feels like we slept for less than an hour.

8
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,879
You don't get it.

9
00:01:48,159 --> 00:01:51,079
Do you know what it means
to sleep with one eye open?

10
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:54,560
I actually don't.

11
00:01:55,439 --> 00:01:56,480
Care to teach me?

12
00:02:01,239 --> 00:02:02,239
Who's there?

13
00:02:03,439 --> 00:02:04,480
Stop hiding.

14
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:05,920
I can see you already.

15
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:10,639
Whose kid is this?

16
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:16,400
I... I don't mean any harm.

17
00:02:17,719 --> 00:02:19,479
I'm just so hungry.

18
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,280
Here.

19
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:32,840
Put this on.

20
00:02:37,639 --> 00:02:38,719
Come warm up by the fire.

21
00:02:41,759 --> 00:02:42,759
What are you afraid of?

22
00:02:43,319 --> 00:02:44,680
If we were bad guys,

23
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,159
we would've eaten you by now.

24
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,360
Come here.

25
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:57,759
It's warm over there.

26
00:03:13,639 --> 00:03:14,719
Eat slowly.

27
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,280
Have some water.

28
00:03:24,319 --> 00:03:26,199
Careful, don't choke.

29
00:03:28,719 --> 00:03:29,960
You can be so gentle.

30
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:31,759
Why are you so ruthless with me?

31
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:33,919
You don't need it.

32
00:03:34,599 --> 00:03:37,199
But she's just a kid.

33
00:03:40,439 --> 00:03:42,999
Do you know how on the border,

34
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,198
those drug dealers and
arms smugglers treat kids?

35
00:03:46,199 --> 00:03:47,599
Kids her age

36
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:49,800
think anyone who feeds
them is a good person.

37
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,880
They're willing to work
for these "good people,"

38
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,680
even if it means

39
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:55,879
becoming their weapons.

40
00:03:58,039 --> 00:03:59,039
I forgot.

41
00:03:59,319 --> 00:04:00,599
You must know this very well.

42
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:02,199
After all,

43
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,719
you're an arms smuggler too.

44
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,080
You've changed from three years ago.

45
00:04:10,319 --> 00:04:11,479
Three years ago,

46
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,800
you said,

47
00:04:14,199 --> 00:04:17,680
"What bad things could a kid
who can't even speak clearly do?"

48
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,240
You saved them

49
00:04:19,879 --> 00:04:21,239
and were proud of it.

50
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,639
Am I the only one who's changed?

51
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:33,120
If it weren't for these things,

52
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,720
these kids

53
00:04:35,199 --> 00:04:37,199
would never have to live like this,

54
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:39,360
and would never do bad things.

55
00:05:38,399 --> 00:05:39,399
Are you cold?

56
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,480
It's time to go.

57
00:05:44,399 --> 00:05:45,799
Do you know how to get out of here?

58
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,479
They searched all night.

59
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,518
Just because they couldn't find us

60
00:05:48,519 --> 00:05:49,719
doesn't mean they've given up.

61
00:05:50,399 --> 00:05:51,399
I don't know.

62
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,560
But we can't stay here anymore.

63
00:05:54,279 --> 00:05:55,480
If they can't find us,

64
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:57,920
they'll come back sooner or later.

65
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,240
Brother.

66
00:06:05,759 --> 00:06:07,240
We have nothing left to give you.

67
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:08,240
Go on your own.

68
00:06:08,241 --> 00:06:09,480
Thank you.

69
00:06:25,399 --> 00:06:26,800
This is the last pack of cookies.

70
00:06:28,879 --> 00:06:30,160
After you leave here,

71
00:06:30,399 --> 00:06:31,879
don't trust anyone so easily.

72
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,760
Not everyone who shares their food with you

73
00:06:33,959 --> 00:06:35,040
is a good person.

74
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,000
But you're a good person, brother.

75
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,279
How about

76
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,839
we take her with us?

77
00:06:43,959 --> 00:06:45,159
With your skills,

78
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,079
adopting a kid

79
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,120
should be a piece of cake.

80
00:06:48,639 --> 00:06:49,839
I don't have what it takes.

81
00:06:50,279 --> 00:06:51,040
Brother,

82
00:06:51,041 --> 00:06:53,959
do you want to go past those
people with the "bang-bangs"?

83
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,720
You sure know a lot.

84
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:58,639
I know a way.

85
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,000
What way?

86
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,199
Don't drag her into this.

87
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:06,159
Just asking.

88
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:07,160
Let's go.

89
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,319
I really do know a way.

90
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,120
This way.

91
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:37,600
I didn't expect this.

92
00:07:38,199 --> 00:07:39,479
You actually dodged the patrol

93
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,480
and made it out.

94
00:07:42,759 --> 00:07:43,759
Give it to me, Mr. Lin.

95
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:46,120
Looks like luck is on our side.

96
00:07:46,279 --> 00:07:46,839
What?

97
00:07:47,079 --> 00:07:48,279
Disappointed?

98
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:51,040
As long as you didn't get him killed.

99
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:51,959
Let's go.

100
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,120
Second Uncle is waiting.

101
00:07:54,279 --> 00:07:55,279
Where's our car?

102
00:07:55,279 --> 00:07:55,920
The car?

103
00:07:56,199 --> 00:07:57,800
Wasn't it your brilliant idea?

104
00:07:57,920 --> 00:07:59,840
It got impounded when
we crashed the checkpoint.

105
00:08:00,279 --> 00:08:01,600
Once past that checkpoint,

106
00:08:02,079 --> 00:08:04,399
here on Hongling Road,
no one stops Lin's cars.

107
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:08,959
Little girl,

108
00:08:09,279 --> 00:08:10,600
we owe you one.

109
00:08:11,079 --> 00:08:12,519
Want to come with Uncle?

110
00:08:12,697 --> 00:08:14,456
We've got plenty of good food

111
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,518
and a big house to live in.

112
00:08:15,519 --> 00:08:16,519
Come on.

113
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,560
Nie Chuan,

114
00:08:18,879 --> 00:08:19,879
for the delivery later,

115
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,199
I'll just go with him.

116
00:08:21,319 --> 00:08:22,319
Outsiders

117
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:23,360
don't need to tag along.

118
00:08:44,279 --> 00:08:45,279
Second Uncle,

119
00:08:45,519 --> 00:08:46,519
the samples are here.

120
00:08:46,799 --> 00:08:47,799
The quantity matches,

121
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
and the quality is solid.

122
00:08:52,159 --> 00:08:53,719
Did everything go smoothly on the road?

123
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,639
We ran into a surprise inspection,

124
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:57,158
but we handled it.

125
00:08:57,159 --> 00:08:58,159
Who handled it?

126
00:08:58,519 --> 00:08:59,519
Nie Chuan.

127
00:09:04,759 --> 00:09:06,439
Near the pickup point,

128
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,759
there was a patrol.

129
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,120
Yeah, he took care of that too.

130
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,320
Black Scorpion,

131
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,799
what do you think?

132
00:09:16,159 --> 00:09:17,159
Second Uncle,

133
00:09:17,679 --> 00:09:19,600
we've been running this
route for over a decade.

134
00:09:19,919 --> 00:09:21,638
The moment he shows
up, things almost go south.

135
00:09:21,639 --> 00:09:23,240
You think he leaked the info?

136
00:09:27,159 --> 00:09:27,879
I think...

137
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:29,799
Who chose this route in the first place?

138
00:09:32,799 --> 00:09:33,878
I think he probably

139
00:09:33,879 --> 00:09:35,000
couldn't have leaked it.

140
00:09:38,639 --> 00:09:39,798
You inspected the goods?

141
00:09:39,799 --> 00:09:40,799
Yes, I did.

142
00:09:40,879 --> 00:09:41,879
No issues.

143
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,960
No issues.

144
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,279
You should check them too.

145
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:57,520
If you've checked them, Second
Uncle, that's good enough.

146
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:59,200
A-yan,

147
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,679
you head back first.

148
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,120
Second Uncle,

149
00:10:09,039 --> 00:10:10,120
about Nie Chuan...

150
00:10:11,159 --> 00:10:12,279
Black Scorpion,

151
00:10:12,919 --> 00:10:14,798
the guide you found

152
00:10:14,799 --> 00:10:16,639
is an ex-mercenary.

153
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:17,840
Did you know that?

154
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:20,759
Second Uncle,

155
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:22,159
it's... it's my fault.

156
00:10:22,679 --> 00:10:24,079
I'll go take care of him right now.

157
00:10:24,759 --> 00:10:25,799
No need.

158
00:10:26,639 --> 00:10:27,919
I trust him.

159
00:10:39,559 --> 00:10:40,759
What do you want to eat today?

160
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,000
You...

161
00:10:47,759 --> 00:10:48,879
Who are you?

162
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:51,480
Why are you in Brother Yan's house?

163
00:10:52,879 --> 00:10:53,879
Who are you?

164
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:55,600
I...

165
00:10:56,039 --> 00:10:58,039
I'm here to see Brother Yan.

166
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,200
Can you...

167
00:10:59,519 --> 00:11:01,360
Can you help me?

168
00:11:16,679 --> 00:11:17,679
Drink some water first.

169
00:11:18,639 --> 00:11:20,639
Are you Brother Yan's friend?

170
00:11:24,399 --> 00:11:25,399
Yes.

171
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:28,480
Then can you help me?

172
00:11:28,799 --> 00:11:29,440
Or,

173
00:11:29,441 --> 00:11:31,038
could you help me find Brother Yan?

174
00:11:31,039 --> 00:11:33,360
Tell me who you are first.

175
00:11:35,039 --> 00:11:36,240
My name is A-ren.

176
00:11:36,639 --> 00:11:37,960
I'm an orphan.

177
00:11:40,879 --> 00:11:42,599
Father took me in

178
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,840
when I was very young.

179
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,559
He treated me very well.

180
00:11:47,519 --> 00:11:49,200
He bought me toys,

181
00:11:49,519 --> 00:11:51,239
dressed me in pretty clothes,

182
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:53,120
and taught me how to read and write.

183
00:11:53,399 --> 00:11:54,399
Father

184
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,399
is also Brother Yan's uncle.

185
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,919
Lin Cang is your father?

186
00:12:01,799 --> 00:12:04,200
Later, when I grew up,

187
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,439
he made me do things

188
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:07,720
I didn't want to do.

189
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,120
I didn't like it.

190
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,440
I didn't want to do it.

191
00:12:10,639 --> 00:12:12,359
Brother Yan said

192
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,720
I should run away.

193
00:12:14,039 --> 00:12:16,240
But now I can't find him.

194
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,440
Brother,

195
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,919
can you take me away?

196
00:12:25,039 --> 00:12:26,359
You can train away the trembling.

197
00:12:27,039 --> 00:12:28,200
You can fake the tears.

198
00:12:29,039 --> 00:12:30,399
But a hand holding the knife

199
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,080
never lies.

200
00:12:38,159 --> 00:12:39,399
Don't move.

201
00:12:41,759 --> 00:12:42,759
Interesting.

202
00:12:46,799 --> 00:12:47,918
Does your Brother Yan know

203
00:12:47,919 --> 00:12:49,120
you came to kill me tonight?

204
00:12:49,799 --> 00:12:51,440
Brother Yan doesn't need to know.

205
00:12:51,919 --> 00:12:53,960
Anyone who stands
between him and our father

206
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,279
must die.

207
00:13:01,039 --> 00:13:02,320
Then do it.

208
00:13:02,919 --> 00:13:05,480
As long as you're not
afraid he'll hate you.

209
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:07,039
You're not going to kill me?

210
00:13:07,799 --> 00:13:09,440
Aren't you A-yan's sister?

211
00:13:09,799 --> 00:13:11,399
I would never hurt his family.

212
00:13:12,679 --> 00:13:14,519
Father will send someone else.

213
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:16,320
Let them come.

214
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,080
A-ren.

215
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,840
He's not your toy.

216
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,199
Brother Yan.

217
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,639
You're angry.

218
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:54,080
Sister.

219
00:13:54,879 --> 00:13:56,200
Staying for dinner?

220
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,360
I'll cook.

221
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,600
Your sister's got some serious skills.

222
00:14:22,039 --> 00:14:23,320
She almost had me.

223
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,080
You didn't have to let her go.

224
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,399
She calls you brother.

225
00:14:29,799 --> 00:14:32,440
How could I lay a hand on her?

226
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:37,600
She's dangerous.

227
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,559
And your current situation

228
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,399
is just as dangerous.

229
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:47,799
More dangerous than you?

230
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,200
Nie Chuan.

231
00:14:53,799 --> 00:14:54,960
I will protect you.

232
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:25,399
The shipment has been handed over.

233
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,639
That was just a sample.

234
00:15:29,919 --> 00:15:31,240
The real deal is yet to come.

235
00:15:32,679 --> 00:15:33,679
So,

236
00:15:33,799 --> 00:15:34,840
that shipment...

237
00:15:35,519 --> 00:15:37,600
Who will it ultimately end up with?

238
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,480
Don't ask questions you shouldn't.

239
00:15:58,519 --> 00:16:00,080
Relax.

240
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:02,039
I'm just curious.

241
00:16:02,279 --> 00:16:03,279
Rebels?

242
00:16:03,639 --> 00:16:04,919
Extremists?

243
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,039
Or some warlord?

244
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:08,320
What exactly are you trying to ask?

245
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:10,720
Lin Yan.

246
00:16:10,919 --> 00:16:12,080
You know better than I do.

247
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:14,000
How long a box of bullets can last.

248
00:16:14,639 --> 00:16:16,279
How many people a batch of guns can kill.

249
00:16:16,639 --> 00:16:17,879
This shipment...

250
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:20,159
How many families will it destroy?

251
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,039
It's not your place to keep that score.

252
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,440
I keep score every day.

253
00:16:24,799 --> 00:16:25,799
Six years ago,

254
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:27,720
what happened in Luoman Village...

255
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:35,320
I always thought it was a
command error from above.

256
00:16:35,759 --> 00:16:37,320
But later I found out

257
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:40,679
those arms dealers

258
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:43,600
would even exploit the elderly
and children in the village.

259
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:45,558
These damn things...

260
00:16:45,559 --> 00:16:47,519
How many people will
they drive to a dead end?

261
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,080
Was I wrong

262
00:16:51,799 --> 00:16:52,919
from the very beginning?

263
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:55,159
Some things just can't be calculated.

264
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,399
So you're just going to

265
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,639
keep playing dumb with me?

266
00:16:58,279 --> 00:16:59,279
Lin Yan.

267
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:00,639
I saw

268
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:02,039
how you treated that kid.

269
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:04,279
You're not that kind of person.

270
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,720
So you can't fool me.

271
00:17:12,799 --> 00:17:13,839
These hands

272
00:17:14,559 --> 00:17:15,920
shouldn't be doing this.

273
00:17:16,039 --> 00:17:19,400
Smuggling guns, moving
cargo, spilling blood...

274
00:17:19,799 --> 00:17:21,039
It doesn't suit them.

275
00:17:35,599 --> 00:17:36,799
That's my cup.

276
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,039
It's all mine.

277
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,480
What are you doing?

278
00:17:47,319 --> 00:17:48,319
This

279
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:52,480
is also mine.

280
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:56,079
Now,

281
00:18:00,839 --> 00:18:01,920
it belongs to me.

282
00:18:03,599 --> 00:18:04,880
What you owe me,

283
00:18:05,319 --> 00:18:06,440
you can pay back with this.

284
00:18:09,039 --> 00:18:10,559
Don't push your luck.

285
00:18:11,039 --> 00:18:12,400
You won't refuse.

286
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,200
You can't bear to.

287
00:19:27,959 --> 00:19:28,959
Enough.

288
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:30,959
Get some rest.

289
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:32,440
What?

290
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:33,080
After all this time,

291
00:19:33,081 --> 00:19:34,319
now you decide to reject me?

292
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,279
It's dangerous here.

293
00:19:37,519 --> 00:19:38,639
I don't care.

294
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:39,640
Don't come any closer.

295
00:19:40,239 --> 00:19:41,519
You'll regret it.

296
00:19:44,319 --> 00:19:45,519
Then let me regret it.

297
00:20:36,319 --> 00:20:37,680
It's late

298
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:38,920
did you get kicked out?

299
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:41,279
Can't I get some fresh air in my own home?

300
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,680
Your own home?

301
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,000
- Take him down.
- Yes, sir.

302
00:20:47,999 --> 00:20:49,038
What is the meaning of this?

303
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:50,039
What meaning?

304
00:20:53,559 --> 00:20:54,599
Let me tell you,

305
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:55,519
letting you live this long

306
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,239
is already my greatest mercy.

307
00:20:57,319 --> 00:20:59,439
Thanks for sparing my life
for so long, Brother Scorpion.

308
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,600
Talking back, huh?

309
00:21:00,799 --> 00:21:01,440
I...

310
00:21:01,799 --> 00:21:02,640
Brother Scorpion,

311
00:21:02,641 --> 00:21:04,080
we still need to report back.

312
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:07,640
True.

313
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:10,920
Take him away.

314
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:17,360
Hurry up.

315
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:52,400
Brother Scorpion,

316
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:54,600
Quite the welcoming committee.

317
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,160
I must be pretty important.

318
00:21:58,039 --> 00:21:59,039
Take him inside.

319
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:11,840
You need a charge to arrest me, right?

320
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,999
You know exactly why.

321
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:19,440
Was there a problem with the last shipment?

322
00:22:21,319 --> 00:22:22,759
Stop playing dumb.

323
00:22:23,279 --> 00:22:24,559
I've already dug up

324
00:22:24,959 --> 00:22:26,998
everything about your background.

325
00:22:26,999 --> 00:22:28,160
Let's hear it then.

326
00:22:29,479 --> 00:22:30,679
You little bastard,

327
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:32,279
still acting tough at death's door.

328
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:35,360
A mercenary pretending to be a guide?

329
00:22:35,719 --> 00:22:37,119
You came to me first.

330
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:38,400
It was a fair trade.

331
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:40,319
But now that Lin Yan controls the route,

332
00:22:40,559 --> 00:22:41,879
and you can't get it,

333
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,319
you're framing me.

334
00:22:43,479 --> 00:22:44,719
If you dare touch me,

335
00:22:45,279 --> 00:22:46,880
Lin Yan won't let you off the hook.
